# A CLI whose home is pointed at a RELATIVE path writes its whole state dir -
# INCLUDING auth.json - into the cwd. That happened once here: a Windows env value
# whose backslashes a shell ate turned GROK_HOME into a relative "D:Programs..."
# and grok dumped 497 files (credentials among them) into the repo. These patterns
# make that mistake inert rather than a shipped credential file.
/Programs*/
/grok-home/
/.grok/
/.minimax/
